[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I made this animation arrive to try the new auto trace and auto weight features and it was so fun. Let me show you how I did it. I started with this idea about the snake and created all the assets I'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'needed for the animation. Then I imported everything into RI and started working on the body. Thinking about animation, I create a'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'simple rig to move the different parts of the body. For the mess, normally what I do is create a new contour and draw the online mess by hand following the'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'image. But this time I try the new autorace option. Let me show you how it works. Now when you select an image and press enter, you have the option auto trace in this vector with a few settings'

[00:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to control how the contour is applied. With detail, you can control how the contour follows the small details. Concavity to control how deeply the'

[01:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'contour follows into a curves. Uniform to control how the vertex are spaced along the contour. alpha to control the transparency result used to detect the'

[01:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'image edge and padding to add an extra space around to the trace outline. With this you can quickly create a contour that follows the shape of the'

[01:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'image and then from here you can move and add more vertex to draw the mess what you need. But remember that the mesh doesn\'t only depend of the shape. It also depends of the animation and the'

[01:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'deformation you want for the shape. So for the snake body, I added a few vertex and draw the interior of the mess following the volume of the body. Once I have them ready, I bend to the'

[01:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'bonds. And now R out of weights the vertex. It\'s a good starting point and you can use the blend option to mix the bones influence and change how many bones can influence each vertex.'

[02:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'There is also a new option I\'ve been waiting for for a long time, smooth, which you can apply to all vertex or only to a selection. Just like the mess, the vertex waiting'

[02:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'depends of the animation and the deformation. So, it\'s normal to edit some weights to make sure everything works as you want. To deform the interior of the body, I nested a new'

[02:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'bone under each body bone and weighted the interior vertex to them. That way, I could move each part of the body and the interior to create a more interesting effect. The snake head was more complex.'

[02:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Here, I created a control to fake a 3D movement. The key was to separate the head into different parts and boil a rig to could move those parts. What I did'

[03:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'was create a group nested under the neck bone. This way I could use the neck bone to move the head and also control the head group itself. Inside I added two'

[03:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'bones, one for the base of the head and the other for the nose and a target to use as a control. Then I weigh the hair to these bones.'

[03:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And to make sure the deformation was what I wanted, I move the control and then change the weights of each vertex to make sure the deformation is right. I'

[03:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'usually do this in a new timeline because I can move the bones without change the rig in the design mode. Once this was working, I did the same with the rest of the elements.'

[03:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'For the hoodie, I added a few bones under the body bones to move it and create a wing effect. To bind the hoodie to the bones, I select both meshes. This is new on drive too. And added all the'

[04:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'bones at the same time. Then I work with the influences to make sure this vertex follow the body and this other vertex follow the hoodie bones. Once I finish it with the snake rig to'

[04:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'connect it to the skateboard, I created a target in the same position of the snake base and nested into the skateboard deck. Then I connected the'

[04:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'base bone to this target using a constraint. So this way the snake move with the skateboard but is not affected by its deformation.'

[04:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Then in the skateboard, I added two bones and create a mess to deform the deck during the animation. For the wheels, I use a simple scale to deform each wheel. And for the spinning effect,'

[04:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I use a stroke on top. The last thing I did was group everything so I could control the entire character from one place. When the character was ready, I started'

[05:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'with the animation. The animation is simple. It\'s based on overlapping loops to create a sense of weight and action reaction. I started with the skateboard because the'

[05:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'character\'s motion depends on it. First, I animate a loop of the deck. Then, I animate the wheels by changing the scale and overlapping the keys a bit'

[05:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to show the wheels reacting to the deck\'s movement. To improve this, I animated the deformation of the deck. Then I did the same with the skateboard'

[05:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'group using a scale. For the body, I create a movement based on the skateboard and overlapping the keys. So each part of the body react to'

[06:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the escapeboard movement. For the head, which the bang of the body movement, I use the nose control. And for the hoodie, I use these bones to'

[06:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'create a reaction of the body movement. To finish, I created this reflection effect to the glasses. For that, I added a vector shape and weighted to the same'

[06:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'bones of the glasses, so it moves in the same way. Then I create another shape with feathering for the light effect and clip it to the shapes.'

[06:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And that\'s it. I hope you like it and that gives you ideas for your next creation.'
